\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces This figure shows the best performing format combo for each of the studied graphs at each K. Each square is also labeled with a speedup over runner up (e.g. 1.1x). There is a broad trend of the best being CSR $\times $ CSR at smaller K, then transitioning to CSC $\times $ CSR or CSC $\times $ COO at larger K. In most cases the difference between CSC $\times $ CSR beating CSC $\times $ COO or vice versa could potentially be contributed to noise as often they are runner ups of each other within 1.1x. 1 Outlier exists with ATP-GR-QC where CSC $\times $ COO beats CSC $\times $ CSR by an average 1.5x. }}{64}{}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:best_for_k}{{6.1}{64}{Outer Product Tie}{figure.6.1}{}}
\def\@LN@column{1}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {subsection}{\numberline {6.4.4}Tiling does not help, at these sizes}{64}{}\protected@file@percent }
\def\@LN@column{1}
